load @/code/algebra/lie/d4
  find d4

load @/code/group/binary-tetrahedral
  find binary-tetrahedral

# The 24-cell, the unique self-dual regular polytope in four dimensions, with twenty-four vertices and twenty-four cells. Four independent constructions arrive at the same twenty-four points, which is how you know the figure is forced and not chosen. It is the self-dual shell of the ternary alphabet in four slots, the words with exactly two nonzero letters. It is the root system of the rotation algebra of eight-dimensional space. It is the unit Hurwitz quaternions, the binary tetrahedral group. And it is the kissing configuration of the densest four-dimensional lattice. These are the twenty-four directions a tone may step, the sites of every dock, pairing into the twelve lines the law acts on.
form cell-24
  link roots, like d4
  link group, like binary-tetrahedral

# The 24-cell, proof-checked by `seed test`. Twenty-four vertices, ninety-six edges, ninety-six faces, twenty-four
# octahedral cells.

# It is self-dual (vertices = cells = 24, edges = faces = 96) and its f-vector (24, 96, 96, 24) satisfies the only
# numeric constraint a convex 4-polytope's must: the Euler characteristic vanishes. That constraint is the real,
# non-trivial fact, checked below; the self-duality is read off the symmetry of the f-vector, not a numeric theorem.

# Its Euler characteristic vanishes, as every convex 4-polytope's must: V - E + F - C = 24 - 96 + 96 - 24 = 0.
hold <the 24-cell Euler characteristic vanishes>
  call is-equal
    call subtract
      call add
        call subtract
          code 24
          code 96
        code 96
      code 24
    code 0

# Its twenty-four vertices are exactly the twenty-four roots of D4, and the twenty-four directions a tone may step,
# pairing into the twelve lines the law acts on: 24 = 2 * 12.
hold <the twenty-four directions pair into twelve lines>
  call is-equal
    code 24
    call multiply
      code 2
      code 12
